lifeos-nix patch f-projects-dormant — do not force-load USER/PROJECTS.md at startup

PROBLEM
  PROJECTS.md is upstream's per-project routing/resume file. Setup step 8
  (activateImports) uncomments its `@`-import in CLAUDE.md, and settings.system.json
  lists it in postCompactRestore.fullFiles — so it is force-loaded at every session
  start AND re-injected in full after every compaction. Unlike the identity files it
  grows UNBOUNDED with project count: on a real multi-project install it measured ~53%
  of startup context (~19.5k tokens) while any given session touches exactly one
  project. That is pure overhead that competes for attention with the rules and
  identity that actually matter. Project/resume state is already available on-demand
  via the ContextSearch skill (session registry + per-project ISAs) and per-project
  CLAUDE.md — the startup force-load duplicates a purpose better served lazily.

FIX (2 files) — change the DEFAULT to dormant, keep it opt-in
  InstallEngine.ts (activateImports) — skip `@LIFEOS/USER/PROJECTS.md`: leave it
  commented in CLAUDE.md instead of uncommenting it. A user who wants PROJECTS.md as a
  startup routing table can uncomment the line by hand; the capability is unchanged,
  only the default. All other identity imports activate as before.
  settings.system.json — drop "USER/PROJECTS.md" from postCompactRestore.fullFiles so
  it is not re-injected after compaction either.

diff --git a/LifeOS/install/skills/LifeOS/Tools/InstallEngine.ts b/LifeOS/install/skills/LifeOS/Tools/InstallEngine.ts
--- a/LifeOS/install/skills/LifeOS/Tools/InstallEngine.ts
+++ b/LifeOS/install/skills/LifeOS/Tools/InstallEngine.ts
@@ -638,6 +638,14 @@
     const m = line.match(commented);
     if (!m) return line;
     const importPath = m[1] || m[2]; // e.g. @LIFEOS/USER/TELOS/PRINCIPAL_TELOS.md
+    // Keep PROJECTS.md dormant (opt-in): it grows unbounded with project count and
+    // dominates startup context (~50%+) while any given session touches one project.
+    // Project/resume state is recalled on-demand via ContextSearch + per-project
+    // ISA/CLAUDE.md. A user who wants it as a startup routing table can uncomment it.
+    if (importPath === "@LIFEOS/USER/PROJECTS.md") {
+      skipped.push(importPath);
+      return line;
+    }
     const rel = importPath.replace(/^@/, "");
     if (existsSync(join(configRoot, rel))) {
       activated.push(importPath);
